## 2. How this report rates risk and maturity

Every AI system in scope is scored with Futran's risk methodology version {{ scoring.version }}{% if scoring.effective_date %}, effective {{ scoring.effective_date }}{% endif %}. The score moves in three steps: how risky the system is by nature (inherent risk), how well its controls work (control maturity), and what risk remains after those controls (residual risk). The residual risk score sets the rating. The full scoring tables are in Appendix A.

### Risk levels

One scale is used for system ratings and finding severities throughout this report. The number in brackets is the level.

| Level | What it means | Residual risk score | Response time |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for l in scoring.levels %}
| {{ l.labelled }} | {{ l.definition | md_cell }} | {{ l.residual_range }} | {{ l.response | md_cell }} |
{% endfor %}

Systems are rated Critical to Low from their residual risk score. Observation is used for findings only. A finding's severity uses the same levels, and its response time sets the default due date for the remediation.

### Inherent risk (0–100)

Inherent risk measures the risk of the system before any controls are considered. It is built from eight factors, each scored 1 to 5 from the questionnaire answers, where 1 is the lowest risk and 5 the highest. Each factor score is converted to points (weight × score ÷ 5 × 100) and the points are added.

| Factor | Weight | 1 (lowest risk) | In between | 5 (highest risk) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for f in scoring.factors %}
