### Knock-out rules and the EU AI Act

A knock-out rule sets a minimum rating whatever the residual score, because the condition is serious on its own.

| Knock-out rule | Minimum rating |
|---|---|
{% for k in scoring.knockouts %}
| {{ k.label | md_cell }} | {{ k.force }} |
{% endfor %}

A system the EU AI Act classifies as high risk has an inherent risk of at least {{ scoring.eu_floor }}, whatever its factor scores. A prohibited practice under the EU AI Act is always rated {{ scoring.eu_prohibited }}. The Lead Auditor may override a computed rating only with a written rationale, which the system profile in section 4 shows.

